LIBRARY Ra3FrameLab
EXPORTS
    FrameLabEnable
    FrameLabDryRun
    FrameLabDisable
    FrameLabStatus
    FrameLabVersion
    FrameLabDumpDiagnostics
    FrameLabSelfTestRollback
    FrameLabSetGroups
    FrameLabMeasureOnly
    FrameLabMeasureOnlyEx
    FrameLabFrameCount
    FrameLabLogicFrame
    FrameLabWaitFrame
    FrameLabFpsWindow
    FrameLabEngineFps
    FrameLabSampleAnim
    FrameLabGateStats
    FrameLabDesyncDump
    FrameLabDesyncRestore
    ; 2026-09-18 batch-11 session (black box: post-mortem for crashes / desyncs).
    ; Existing logs only cover INSTALL time (signature hits, patched bytes, rollback),
    ; so a crash or a desync left nothing behind -- no scene, only guessing.
    ; FrameLabBlackBox(on) toggles the flight recorder (per-render-frame ring buffer).
    ; FrameLabBlackBoxDump() writes the current scene to logs\snapshot-*.log right now.
    ; FrameLabBlackBoxLast(buf,cap) returns the path of the most recent report.
    ; FrameLabBlackBoxSelfTest() walks the REAL vectored-exception path with a custom
    ; exception code swallowed by its own __try/__except, so it proves the handler
    ; actually writes a file without crashing the game.
    FrameLabBlackBox
    FrameLabBlackBoxDump
    FrameLabBlackBoxLast
    FrameLabBlackBoxSelfTest
    ; 2026-09-17 animation-ruler session: three new read-only exports.
    ; ASCII ONLY -- do not put non-ASCII bytes in this file. It was written with UTF-8
    ; Chinese comments once and link.exe (which reads .def in the ANSI codepage) then
    ; silently dropped the line that followed, so FrameLabAnimRate fell back to
    ; __declspec(dllexport)'s __stdcall decoration and shipped as "_FrameLabAnimRate@4".
    ; flctl's GetProcAddress("FrameLabAnimRate") then failed and read/animrate returned
    ; -9999. tools/re/check_exports.sh now verifies the export table after every build.
    FrameLabAnimRate
    FrameLabAnimReset
    ; 2026-09-18 batch-11 session (animation slots, read-only): dump ALL 12 animation
    ; slots the anim ruler has registered, not just the first 4 that the black box
    ; records. Measured evidence: the "cut animation" hook runs ~24 times/second, yet
    ; the first 4 slots all held STATIC objects (score constant for the whole window).
    ; Call it TWICE about 1 second apart and compare the "current" column -- the slot
    ; whose value moves is the object that is actually animating.
    FrameLabAnimSlots
    ; 2026-09-18 batch-11 session (world-coordinate scan, read-only). The user answered
    ; the two triage questions: "vanilla is slight, patched is clearly worse" and
    ; "jitters while MOVING, steady when standing still" -- so the problem is on the
    ; POSITION path, not on animation mixing (animation runs while standing too).
    ; But the project has no instrument that can read a unit's WORLD COORDINATES, and
    ; the three quantities we CAN read (frac / logic advance / game clock) are all
    ; bit-identical to vanilla at 30 fps. So: enumerate writable memory, keep
    ; three-adjacent-float triples that look like world coordinates, sleep 1 s,
    ; re-read them, and print only the ones that MOVED. This finds the moving units
    ; WITHOUT reversing the object graph. Output is a string, so it needs a buffer.
    FrameLabMemScan
    ; 2026-09-18 batch-11 session (world-coordinate TRACKING). memscan finds the address of
    ; a moving triple once; those addresses change every run and a single snapshot cannot
    ; show whether the value JITTERS. FrameLabTrack(addr) hands one address to the black
    ; box, which then records its three floats once per render frame. This is the only
    ; direct read of "the vehicle bobs up and down" -- the time-axis instruments cannot
    ; see position, and neither can the animation-score channels.
    ; addr = 0 clears the channel. Returns 0 on success, -1 if the address is rejected.
    FrameLabTrack
    FrameLabReadDword
    FrameLabClockPerLogicFrame
    ; 2026-09-17 clock-accumulator session: offline check for the ms-per-frame
    ; accumulator. Pure integer arithmetic on our own globals, so it runs without
    ; the game and without a game process (tests/test_loader.cpp calls it).
    FrameLabSelfTestClock
    ; 2026-09-17 acceptance-criteria session: in-process logic frame rate (fps*100).
    ; This is the precise form of "the simulation still runs at 15 Hz", which is the
    ; definition of "90 fps without changing the sim". FrameLabEngineFps cannot serve:
    ; it reads the engine's exponentially-smoothed display value and lags behind.
    FrameLabLogicFps
    ; 2026-09-17 P6b session: the objective ruler for the SECOND animation time path
    ; (sub_903910 -> sub_8EA220, dt = frame-delta / client-fps). clockrate/animrate only
    ; see the game-clock path, so they cannot show whether P6b took effect. Returns
    ; "animation milliseconds advanced per logic frame" x1000: 66667 = correct at any fps.
    FrameLabBlendStepPerLogicFrame
    ; 2026-09-17 batch-7 session (building-animation root cause): read-only ruler that
    ; measures the DISPLAY frame counter rate -- vtbl[116](dword_CDB750), the same counter
    ; that sub_6F6CB0 (module "StructureUnpackUpdate", the building unpack/build-up
    ; animation) divides by (duration_ms * flt_CDBC5C). Everything in the derived-constant
    ; fix hinges on that rate, so it is measured rather than assumed. Also prints the
    ; current values of 0xCDBC50 / 0xCDBC54 / 0xCDBC5C. Returns frames/second (or <0).
    FrameLabDisplayClock
    ; 2026-09-21 chassis-suspension session. The vehicle body pose (suspension bounce,
    ; pitch, roll, visual Z) comes from a CLIENT-side chain that none of the earlier
    ; rulers can see: sub_53F080 Drawable::draw -> sub_535DD0 applyPhysicsXform ->
    ; sub_532CA0 calcPhysicsXform -> sub_526BD0 / sub_51E800 / sub_5262D0. It is a set of
    ; per-DISPLAY-frame recurrences with no dt, so at 60/90 fps the body motion runs
    ; 2x/3x fast. Hook = the single `call sub_532CA0` at 0x00535E87 (rel32 retarget).
    ; Groups 0x80000 (read-only probe) and 0x100000 (30 Hz cadence gate), BOTH default off.
    ; FrameLabChassisRate(logicFrames): recurrence steps per logic frame x1000 for the
    ;   busiest on-screen vehicle. 2000 = vanilla / fixed; 4000 / 6000 = unfixed 60 / 90.
    ;   -1 = no usable data, -2 = wrapper not installed (not the same thing).
    ; FrameLabChassisSlots(buf): table dump (drawable, locomotor appearance, counters,
    ;   last pitch/roll/yaw/z). Needs an output buffer, like FrameLabAnimSlots.
    ; FrameLabSelfTestChassis(): offline self-test of the gate logic (pure arithmetic on a
    ;   private table with a fake spring recurrence; no game needed). 0xFF = all pass.
    ; FrameLabChassisStatus(): -2 = wrapper not installed, 0 = probe only, 1 = gate (hold),
    ;   2 = gate (interpolation). Lets the GUI say whether the fix actually engaged.
    FrameLabChassisStatus
    ; 2026-09-21: user-selectable scroll-speed normalisation (group 0x800000, default off).
    ; FrameLabScrollStatus(): -2 = patch points not found, 0 = off, 1 = engaged.
    FrameLabScrollStatus
    ; 2026-09-22: tracer-stream 30 Hz cadence gate (group 0x1000000, default off).
    ; FrameLabTracerStatus(): -2 = patch point missing, 0 = off, 1000000+ratio = engaged
    ;   (ratio = forwarded/called x1000; ~333 at 90 fps, ~500 at 60 fps).
    FrameLabTracerStatus
    ; 2026-09-23: particle-system manager 30 Hz cadence gate (group 0x4000000, default off).
    ; FrameLabPsysStatus(): -2 = patch point missing, 0 = off, 1000000+ratio = engaged.
    FrameLabPsysStatus
    ; 2026-09-26: scripted-camera timing fix (group 0x8000000, default off).
    ; FrameLabCameraStatus(): -2 = not all 16 sites patched, 0 = off / not needed, 1000+ms = engaged.
    FrameLabCameraStatus
    FrameLabChassisRate
    FrameLabChassisSlots
    FrameLabSelfTestChassis
